hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"190","Bārakallāhu lak, wa bāraka `alayk, wa jama`a baynakumā fī khayr. May Allah bless you, and shower His blessings upon you, and join you together in goodness. Reference: Abu Dawud, Ibn Majah and At-Tirmidhi. See also Al-Albani, Sahih At-Tirmidhi 1/316."
"191","Idhā tazawwaja aḥadukumu imra’atan, aw idhā ishtarā khādiman fal-yaqul: (Allāhumma innī as’aluka khayrahā, wa khayra mā jabaltahā ‘alayhi, wa a‘ūdhu bika min sharrahā, wa sharri mā jabaltahā ‘alayhi), wa idhā ishtarā ba‘īran fal-ya’khudh bi-dhirwati sanāmihi wal-yaqul mithla dhālik.. When one of you marries a woman, or when he buys a servant, let him say: \O Allah"","" I ask You for her goodness and the goodness of what You have created her upon"","" and I seek refuge in You from her evil and the evil of what You have created her upon.\"" And if he buys a camel"","" let him hold the top of its hump and say the same."""""
